# OpenClaw's own guidance (seen live in its doctor output on first run,
# 2026-10-09): "back up the agent workspace in a private git repo; keep
# ~/.openclaw out of git (credentials, sessions)." The real runtime
# config/state directory never lives in this repo at all (it's on a
# persistent EFS volume in production, see README.md) - these entries
# are for anyone who runs the container locally against a bind-mounted
# directory for testing.
.openclaw/
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-journal
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Local test volumes if you mount one at this path when running
# `docker run -v` locally, per README.md's dry-run instructions.
local-state/

# Standard OS/editor noise.
.DS_Store
*.log
